<title>UK: Cairn rallies on director stock purchases.</title>
<headline>Cairn rallies on director stock purchases.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Cairn Energy Plc rebounded on Wednesday, having been in a downtrend for the last three months, on news that five of the company's directors purchased stock, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1109 GMT, the shares were up 21p at 487-1/2.  </p>
<p>The directors today purchased a total 24,757 ordinary shares at 475p per share, according to a statement from the company.</p>
<p>Dealers said the market had been oversold and news of the purchases helped galvanise the rally.</p>
<p>The stock hit a 5-1/2-month low on Tuesday, having tumbled 177p, or about 28 percent, from its March 19 high at 640p.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
